# --- local build / verification scratch (never part of the app) ---------------
# Build output: the release APK and the Gradle/Metro logs are produced locally
# and are far too large to version. The APK is attached to a GitHub Release
# instead of committed.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_*
*.dex
apk-build.log
apk-run.log
apk-build-run.log
build-*.log
/out/

# Gradle / JVM toolchain written into the project by the local Android build
.gradle-home/
.gradle-tmp/
.jvmtest/
.jvmtest-export/
.gradle/
build/

# --- the behaviour gates are SOURCE, not scratch --------------------------------
#
# The `.bench/` directory used to be ignored wholesale, on the reasoning that it held harnesses and
# their scratch bundles. That reasoning was wrong, and it was wrong in the direction that matters:
# `.bench/` is where every one of GATE 1c-a through 1n lives, and `scripts/build-apk.sh` REFUSES TO
# BUILD unless they pass. A build gate that is not in version control is a gate that only exists on
# the machine that wrote it, and this project's whole defence against its own recurring bugs is that
# a check runs on every build.
#
# So the tests are tracked and the SCRATCH is not. The split is by kind, and it is worth writing down
# because the previous rule deleted both:
#
#   tracked  - *.test.mjs, which is every gate `build-apk.sh` runs.
#   ignored  - probe/audit/fix/one-off scripts, their output, their caches, scratch bundles and
#              reports, and the generated corpus snapshots.
#
# `scripts/bundlecheck.py` is NOT here — it lives in `scripts/`, is already tracked, and is the
# GATE 2 needle list. An earlier version of this comment claimed otherwise, which is the sort of
# thing that reads as a fact and is not; it was written before the file was looked for.
#
# `!.bench/*.test.mjs` is what re-includes the gates after the catch-all, and the ORDER matters: git
# applies the LAST matching pattern, so the negation has to come after the catch-all. A misplaced
# negation looks correct in review and silently un-commits the checks, which is why the gates'
# presence in the repository is asserted by a check rather than by eye.
.bench/*
!.bench/*.test.mjs
!.bench/test-games.json
*.bench.js
*.bench.cjs
*-check.json

# Stray Windows path artifact from a bad %SystemDrive% expansion during a build
%SystemDrive%/

# Stale local backups (e.g. an old inlined-wasm assets.ts) must never be tracked
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*~

# AI-assistant scratch files are not part of the app
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/

# On-device debug artefacts. `adb shell screencap` and `uiautomator dump` are how the
# board and its touch target get verified on a real phone, and both land in the repo
# root. They are per-session evidence, not source: a 500 kB screenshot of whatever
# screen happened to be open tells the next reader nothing and bloats every diff.
shot-*.png
ui-*.xml
ui-now.xml

# Per-session Gradle/Metro run logs. `build-*.log` covered three of the names this project had
# accumulated; rather than add a line per new name, the whole family goes.
*-run.log
*-run2.log
*-run3.log

# Generated by scripts/build-engine-harness.mjs - real Stockfish WASM, 7 MB, rebuilt not committed.
# The gate prints the command to run if it is missing, which is better than a silent skip.
.bench/harness.html
.bench/harness.wasm

# Per-session device-driving helpers. `adb shell input tap` is how the board gets verified on a real
# phone, and these wrap it. They are machine-specific - each hard-codes a device serial and a path to
# the Android SDK - so committing them would put one person's phone into everyone's checkout, and the
# next reader would have no way to use it without editing it first. The scripts they wrap (`adb`) are
# the durable part.
scripts/drive.ps1
scripts/tap.ps1
scripts/walk.ps1
scripts/ensure.ps1

# Scratch written next to the file under test by a gate that was interrupted mid-run.
*.tmp
# Local gate / build logs
.gates.log
.apk-build.log

# Scratch directories for the marketing build (`scripts/build-marketing.py`) and the
# on-device screen captures: cropped frames, raw phone shots, intermediate encodes and
# QA stills. The published artwork lives in docs/marketing, not here.
.tmp-*/
docs/.tmp-demo/
__pycache__/
